NNAAMMEE
       pppdump - convert PPP record file to readable format

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppppppdduummpp [ --hh | --pp [ --dd ]] [ --rr ] [ --aa ] [ --mm _m_r_u ] [ _f_i_l_e ...  ]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ppppppdduummpp utility converts the files written using the _r_e_c_o_r_d option
       of ppppppdd into a human‐readable format.  If one  or  more  filenames  are
       specified,  ppppppdduummpp  will read each in turn; otherwise it will read its
       standard input.  In each case the result is written to standard output.

       The options are as follows:

       --hh     Prints the bytes sent and received in hexadecimal.   If  neither
              this  option  nor  the  --pp  option  is  specified, the bytes are
              printed as the characters themselves, with non‐printing and non‐
              ASCII characters printed as escape sequences.

       --pp     Collects the bytes sent and received into  PPP  packets,  inter‐
              preting  the async HDLC framing and escape characters and check‐
              ing the FCS (frame check sequence) of each packet.  The  packets
              are printed as hex values and as characters (non‐printable char‐
              acters are printed as ‘.’).

       --dd     With  the  --pp  option,  this option causes ppppppdduummpp to decompress
              packets which have been compressed with the BSD‐Compress or  De‐
              flate methods.

       --rr     Reverses the direction indicators, so that ‘sent’ is printed for
              bytes  or  packets  received, and ‘rcvd’ is printed for bytes or
              packets sent.

       --aa     Prints absolute times.

       --mm _m_r_u Use _m_r_u as the MRU (maximum receive unit) for both directions of
              the link when checking for over‐length PPP packets (with the  --pp
              option).

